{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing PostgreSQL Service Container in CircleCI Job",
    "Explanation": [
      "The config declares only a single docker image (circleci/node) with no secondary service container for PostgreSQL. The log shows dockerize successfully installed and running, but every dial to 127.0.0.1:5432 returns 'connection refused' for the full 60 seconds — nothing is listening on that port because no database was ever started. This rules out dockerize being missing (it ran), the timeout being too short (connection refused is immediate rejection, not slow startup), the wrong port (5432 is the standard PostgreSQL port), and a missing client library (the check is a raw TCP dial). The fix is to add a PostgreSQL service image (e.g., circleci/postgres) as a second entry under the job's docker key so the database is available on localhost:5432 before the wait step runs."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_postgres_service_image\",",
      "  \"root_cause\": \"no_postgres_service_container\"",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_postgres_service_image\",",
        "  \"root_cause\": \"no_postgres_service_container\"",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
