{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing Test Results and Artifact Publication",
    "Explanation": [
      "The run step writes a valid JUnit XML file to ~/project/results/test_results.xml (confirmed by the log line 'Wrote ~/project/results/test_results.xml'), so results are produced. However, the step ends with 'exit 1', and the log shows 'Exited with code exit status 1' / 'CircleCI received exit code 1', so the job is red, not green. The config contains no store_test_results step, so nothing populates the test summary tab, and it contains no store_artifacts step, so the results file is not available as an artifact. Both are missing. To satisfy the requirement (same file in test summary tab AND as an artifact), the fix is to add both store_test_results (path: ~/project/results) and store_artifacts (path: ~/project/results) after the run step. 'set_upload_true' is not a real CircleCI mechanism, and adding only one of the two steps or only removing the exit 1 would not meet the stated requirement. Removing exit 1 would additionally make the job green, but the publication fix is the required change; note that store_test_results/store_artifacts still run on failure if the step precedes or uses when: always semantics appropriately (these steps run even when a prior step fails? No—by default subsequent steps are skipped after a failed run step, so removing the forced exit 1 or using when: always would also be needed for upload in practice), but the schema fix option addressing the requirement is adding both store steps."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
      "  \"job_green\": false,",
      "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
      "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
      "  \"results_produced\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
        "  \"job_green\": false,",
        "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
        "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
        "  \"results_produced\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
