{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy job missing production branch filter",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow ran on branch 'koans-08-branch-filters', not 'production', yet the deploy job executed and succeeded. The pipeline is green (all jobs SUCCESS), but the behaviour violates the requirement that deploy run only on the production branch. The workflow config has no branch filters at all; deploy only has 'requires: test-production', which controls ordering, not branch eligibility. The fix is to add a 'filters: branches: only: production' block to the deploy job entry in the workflow's jobs list, since branch eligibility is controlled at the workflow job level."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
