{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Beta Tag Filters Missing on All Jobs",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen workflow.txt shows pipeline #156 with workflow build-test-and-deploy SUCCESS and all three jobs (build, test, deploy) succeeding, so the pipeline is green. However, the frozen config.yml contains no `filters` on any job in the workflow. In CircleCI, jobs without tag filters never run for tag pushes, so the required beta-tagged release flow would not execute at all, while deploy currently runs on every branch commit (this run was an API trigger on the koans-09-tag-filters branch). The behaviour therefore does not match the requirement. Because CircleCI requires that every job upstream of a tag-filtered job also carry tag filters (deploy requires test, test requires build), the tag filter must be applied to all three jobs in the workflow, not just deploy. The correct configuration is `filters: tags: only: /^beta-.*/` (with `branches: ignore: /.*/` for a tag-only flow) on build, test, and deploy, so only beta tags trigger the flow and non-beta tags do not."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
